' =====================================================================
' RoboFetch - C2, order admission (SIMPLIFIED for understanding)
'
' Drops the reservation-ledger internals and the exact wording of each
' refusal to show just the CONCEPT: four hard physical/business checks,
' in cheapest-and-most-certain-first order, then one learned opinion
' layered on top that can only ever refuse, never approve, what the
' hard checks already allowed. See 05-activity-admission.puml for the
' exact gates, in the exact order the code runs them.
' =====================================================================
@startuml
skinparam backgroundColor White
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam activity {
  BackgroundColor #FBFCFE
  BorderColor #34495E
  ArrowColor #34495E
  DiamondBackgroundColor #FDF6E3
  DiamondBorderColor #34495E
}

start
:Someone orders a product;

if (Is it in stock?) then (no)
  :REFUSE;
  stop
endif

if (Would the robot still have\nenough battery to get home?) then (no)
  :REFUSE;
  stop
endif

if (Would the motors overheat?) then (no)
  :REFUSE;
  stop
endif

if (Is the robot healthy enough\nto work at all?) then (no)
  :REFUSE;
  stop
endif

note right
  4 hard, certain checks -
  no judgment needed, just
  physics and facts.
end note

if (What does the learned\nmodel think?) then (risky)
  :REFUSE;
  stop
else (looks fine)
endif

note right
  1 learned opinion, added
  LAST - it can only refuse a
  job the 4 checks already
  allowed, never approve one
  they rejected.
end note

:ACCEPT the order;
stop

@enduml
